LESSON 17: PROPS AND ONE-WAY DATA FLOW - OVERVIEW
================================================================================

Key Concepts:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
• One-Way Flow
  - Data flows from parent → child

• Props Channel
  - Props carry data downward

• Functions as Props
  - Child can invoke a function supplied by the parent

• Predictability
  - Makes data changes easier to trace


Data Flow Pattern:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Parent owns state

function Parent() {
  const [count, setCount] = useState(0)

  return (
    <Child
      count={count}
      onIncrement={() => setCount(count + 1)}
    />
  )
}


// Child receives data and function

function Child({ count, onIncrement }) {
  return (
    <div>
      <p>Count: {count}</p>
      <button onClick={onIncrement}>
        Increment
      </button>
    </div>
  )
}


Data Flow:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Parent State
    ↓
Props
    ↓
Child Component
    ↓
User Action
    ↓
Parent Function
    ↓
State Update
    ↓
UI Re-render


