PART 6: MISTAKES TO AVOID
================================================================================

MISTAKE 1: MODIFYING PROPS DIRECTLY
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// ❌ Wrong

function Book(props) {
  props.title = 'New Title'
}


// ✓ Correct

function Book({ title }) {
  return <h2>{title}</h2>
}

Reason:
Props are read-only inputs received from the parent.


================================================================================
MISTAKE 2: USING INDEX AS KEY
================================================================================

// ❌ Risky when list items can reorder/change

{items.map((item, index) => (
  <Item key={index} item={item} />
))}


// ✓ Preferred

{items.map(item => (
  <Item key={item.id} item={item} />
))}

Reason:
A stable unique ID lets React consistently identify an item.


================================================================================
MISTAKE 3: FORGETTING THE KEY PROP
================================================================================

// ❌ Wrong

{items.map(item => (
  <Item item={item} />
))}


// ✓ Correct

{items.map(item => (
  <Item key={item.id} item={item} />
))}


================================================================================
MISTAKE 4: NOT DESTRUCTURING PROPS
================================================================================

// Less clean

function Book(props) {
  return <h2>{props.title}</h2>
}


// Cleaner

function Book({ title }) {
  return <h2>{title}</h2>
}


